<BaseLayout
	title="Philippine Highway Kilometer Post & KM 0 Marker Locator — mapaPH Tools"
	description="Interactive locator and visualizer for Philippine Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) concrete kilometer posts and official Kilometer Zero monuments. Search milestone markers along MacArthur Highway, Maharlika Highway, Marilaque Highway (Rizal), Manila East Road, Aguinaldo Highway, Kennon Road, and the Bataan Death March."
	keywords="Philippine kilometer post finder, KM 0 Manila Luneta, Philippine highway markers, DPWH kilometer posts, Marilaque highway km posts, Manila East Road Rizal, MacArthur Highway km posts, Maharlika Highway km markers, Bataan Death March km markers, distance from Luneta KM 0, how to read Philippine KM posts"
>
	<!-- Leaflet Stylesheet -->
	<link
		rel="stylesheet"
		href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
		integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
		crossorigin=""
		slot="schema"
	/>

	<script type="application/ld+json" slot="schema" is:inline>
		{
			"@context": "https://schema.org",
			"@graph": [
				{
					"@type": "WebApplication",
					"name": "Philippine Highway Kilometer Post & KM 0 Marker Locator",
					"url": "https://mapaph.com/tools/kilometer-posts",
					"applicationCategory": "Geographic Reference & Highway Utility",
					"operatingSystem": "All",
					"description": "Interactive search and visualization utility for DPWH highway milestone posts and regional Kilometer Zero geodetic benchmarks across the Philippines.",
					"provider": {
						"@type": "Organization",
						"name": "mapaPH",
						"url": "https://mapaph.com"
					}
				},
				{
					"@type": "BreadcrumbList",
					"itemListElement": [
						{
							"@type": "ListItem",
							"position": 1,
							"name": "Home",
							"item": "https://mapaph.com"
						},
						{
							"@type": "ListItem",
							"position": 2,
							"name": "Tools",
							"item": "https://mapaph.com/tools"
						},
						{
							"@type": "ListItem",
							"position": 3,
							"name": "Kilometer Post Locator",
							"item": "https://mapaph.com/tools/kilometer-posts"
						}
					]
				}
			]
		}
	</script>

	<Navbar />

	<main class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-14 text-mapa-ink">
		<!-- Header Breadcrumb & Tag -->
		<div class="mb-8">
			<nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-sans text-mapa-clay mb-3">
				<a href="/" class="hover:text-mapa-green transition-colors">Home</a>
				<span>/</span>
				<a href="/tools" class="hover:text-mapa-green transition-colors">Tools</a>
				<span>/</span>
				<span class="text-mapa-ink font-semibold">Kilometer Posts</span>
			</nav>

			<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5">
				<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-mapa-green/15 text-mapa-green border border-mapa-green/30">
					DPWH National Road Milestones
				</span>
				<span class="text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour text-mapa-ink/75">
					Kilometer Zero Geodetic Benchmarks
				</span>
				<span class="text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-800 border border-amber-500/20">
					Civilian & Survey Reference
				</span>
			</div>

			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-mapa-green font-serif tracking-tight mt-3">
				Philippine Kilometer Post & KM 0 Locator
			</h1>
			<p class="font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-mapa-ink/80 mt-2.5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
				Search, calculate, and inspect concrete DPWH highway milestone posts across the Philippines. Locate physical distance markers from Luzon's Kilometer Zero in Luneta, Marilaque Highway across Rizal and the Sierra Madre, Manila East Road, Mindanao KM 0, and provincial origins.
			</p>
		</div>

		<!-- Regional KM 0 Origin Benchmark Switcher Cards -->
		<section class="mb-10 font-sans">
			<div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-4 border-b border-mapa-contour/50">
				<div>
					<h2 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-mapa-ink">
						Philippine Kilometer Zero (KM 0) Benchmarks
					</h2>
					<p class="text-xs text-mapa-clay">
						Select a regional origin point to inspect its history and surveying coordinates.
					</p>
				</div>
				<span class="text-xs text-mapa-clay hidden sm:block">Geodetic Origins</span>
			</div>

			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-3">
				{KM_ZERO_ORIGINS.map((origin, index) => (
					<button
						type="button"
						id={`btn-origin-${origin.id}`}
						data-origin-id={origin.id}
						class={`origin-select-card text-left p-4 rounded-xl border transition-all cursor-pointer ${
							index === 0
								? 'bg-mapa-canvas-dark border-mapa-green shadow-2xs ring-1 ring-mapa-green/30'
								: 'bg-mapa-canvas-dark border-mapa-contour hover:border-mapa-green/40'
						}`}
					>
						<span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-green">
							KM 0 Benchmark
						</span>
						<h3 class="font-serif text-sm font-bold text-mapa-ink mt-1">
							{origin.name.split('(')[0].trim()}
						</h3>
						<span class="text-[11px] text-mapa-clay block mt-0.5 truncate">
							{origin.location.split(',')[0]}
						</span>
					</button>
				))}
			</div>

			<!-- Active Origin Detail Banner -->
			<div id="origin-detail-banner" class="mt-4 p-5 rounded-2xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/80 shadow-xs">
				<div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-mapa-contour/50 pb-4 mb-3">
					<div>
						<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
							<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-mapa-green/15 text-mapa-green">
								Active Origin
							</span>
							<h3 id="origin-banner-title" class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-mapa-ink">
								{KM_ZERO_ORIGINS[0].name}
							</h3>
						</div>
						<p id="origin-banner-location" class="text-xs text-mapa-clay mt-1">
							{KM_ZERO_ORIGINS[0].location}
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-xs">
						<div class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour">
							<span class="text-[10px] text-mapa-clay uppercase font-bold block">Coordinates</span>
							<span id="origin-banner-coords" class="font-mono font-bold text-mapa-ink">14.5826° N, 120.9787° E</span>
						</div>
						<div class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour">
							<span class="text-[10px] text-mapa-clay uppercase font-bold block">Elevation</span>
							<span id="origin-banner-elevation" class="font-mono font-bold text-mapa-ink">3 m ASL</span>
						</div>
						<a
							id="origin-banner-ref-link"
							href={KM_ZERO_ORIGINS[0].refUrl}
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							class="px-3 py-2 rounded-lg bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour hover:border-mapa-green text-mapa-ink font-semibold text-xs transition-all shadow-2xs flex items-center gap-1.5 cursor-pointer"
							title="View official registry record confirming this marker"
						>
							<span>🏛️</span>
							<span id="origin-banner-ref-label">{KM_ZERO_ORIGINS[0].refName}</span>
							<svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-mapa-clay" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
								<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" />
							</svg>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 pt-2">
					<p id="origin-banner-history" class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed flex-1">
						{KM_ZERO_ORIGINS[0].history}
					</p>
					<span id="origin-banner-badge" class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour text-[11px] font-bold text-mapa-green shrink-0">
						{KM_ZERO_ORIGINS[0].markerBadge}
					</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Main Interactive Tool Section: 2 Columns (Controls + Concrete Post 3D/SVG Visualizer & Dual Visualizer) -->
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start mb-12 font-sans">
			
			<!-- Left Column: Highway Corridor Selector, KM Post Slider, and Concrete Milestone Visualizer (5 cols) -->
			<div class="lg:col-span-5 flex flex-col gap-6">
				<!-- Control Panel Card -->
				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-xs">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-mapa-ink border-b border-mapa-contour/50 pb-3 mb-5">
						Milestone Post Inspector
					</h2>

					<!-- Select Highway Corridor -->
					<div class="space-y-4">
						<div>
							<label for="corridor-select" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-clay mb-1.5">
								Select Highway Trunk / Memorial Corridor
							</label>
							<select
								id="corridor-select"
								class="w-full bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-mapa-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-mapa-green/40 cursor-pointer"
							>
								{HIGHWAY_CORRIDORS.map((corridor, idx) => (
									<option value={corridor.id} selected={idx === 0}>
										{corridor.name} ({corridor.region})
									</option>
								))}
							</select>
						</div>

						<!-- Milestone Slider & Direct KM Input -->
						<div>
							<div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1.5">
								<label for="km-slider" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-clay">
									Milestone Marker Post
								</label>
								<div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
									<span class="text-xs font-bold text-mapa-green">KM</span>
									<input
										type="number"
										id="km-number-input"
										min="0"
										max="488"
										value="66"
										class="w-16 px-2 py-1 text-center font-mono font-bold text-sm bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour rounded-lg text-mapa-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-mapa-green"
									/>
								</div>
							</div>

							<input
								type="range"
								id="km-slider"
								min="0"
								max="488"
								value="66"
								step="1"
								class="w-full h-2 bg-mapa-contour rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-mapa-green"
							/>

							<div class="flex justify-between text-[11px] text-mapa-clay mt-1">
								<span id="slider-min-label">KM 0 (Luneta)</span>
								<span id="slider-max-label">KM 488 (Laoag)</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Visual Concrete Milestone Post (Graphic Representation) -->
					<div class="mt-6 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-b from-mapa-canvas to-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
						<span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-clay mb-3">
							DPWH Standard Concrete Marker
						</span>

						<!-- Concrete Post Graphic Container -->
						<div class="relative w-44 bg-slate-100 rounded-t-3xl border-4 border-slate-300 shadow-md flex flex-col items-center overflow-hidden">
							<!-- Rounded Top Arch Cap -->
							<div class="w-full bg-slate-200/80 py-2 border-b-2 border-slate-300 text-center">
								<div id="post-dest-name" class="font-sans font-extrabold text-slate-800 text-xs tracking-wider">
									ANGELES 17
								</div>
							</div>

							<!-- Center Post Body with Kilometer Text -->
							<div class="py-6 px-4 text-center">
								<div class="text-[11px] font-extrabold tracking-widest text-slate-500">KM</div>
								<div id="post-km-number" class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 font-mono tracking-tight">
									66
								</div>
							</div>

							<!-- Red DPWH Concrete Base Band -->
							<div class="w-full bg-rose-700 text-white text-center py-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold border-t-2 border-rose-900">
								<span id="post-road-code">N2 &bull; DPWH REGION III</span>
							</div>
						</div>

						<p class="text-[11px] text-mapa-clay mt-3 text-center">
							Physical monument located along highway right-of-way
						</p>
					</div>

					<!-- Computed Marker Location Details -->
					<div id="active-marker-card" class="mt-5 p-4 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour text-xs space-y-2.5">
						<div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-mapa-contour/50 pb-2">
							<span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-clay">Location Status</span>
							<span id="marker-town-badge" class="font-bold text-mapa-green">San Fernando City, Pampanga</span>
						</div>
						<div>
							<span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-clay block">Prominent Landmark</span>
							<p id="marker-landmark" class="text-mapa-ink/85 mt-0.5">Pampanga Provincial Capitol, San Fernando Train Station</p>
						</div>
						<div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-center pt-1 text-[11px] text-mapa-clay gap-2">
							<span>Highway Code: <strong id="marker-route-code" class="text-mapa-ink">N2 / MacArthur Hwy</strong></span>
							<span>Approx. Coords: <strong id="marker-coords" class="font-mono text-mapa-ink">15.0300° N, 120.6900° E</strong></span>
						</div>
						<div id="marker-gmaps-container" class="pt-2 border-t border-mapa-contour/40">
							<a
								id="marker-gmaps-link"
								href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kilometer+Zero+Rizal+Park+Manila"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer"
								class="w-full py-2 px-3 rounded-lg bg-emerald-600/10 hover:bg-emerald-600 text-emerald-800 hover:text-white font-semibold text-xs border border-emerald-600/30 transition-all flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 cursor-pointer shadow-2xs"
								title="Open verified milestone location in Google Maps"
							>
								<span>📍 Open Real-Life Location in Google Maps</span>
								<svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
									<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" />
								</svg>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column: Dual Visualizer (Schematic Milestone Chain vs Geographic Map) (7 cols) -->
			<div class="lg:col-span-7 flex flex-col gap-4">
				<!-- Visualizer Controls: View Mode Switcher -->
				<div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-2xl p-3.5 shadow-2xs">
					<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
						<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-clay pl-2">Display View:</span>
						<div class="inline-flex rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas p-1 border border-mapa-contour">
							<button
								id="btn-view-schematic"
								type="button"
								class="px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold rounded-lg bg-mapa-green text-white shadow-2xs transition-all cursor-pointer"
							>
								Milestone Chain
							</button>
							<button
								id="btn-view-geo"
								type="button"
								class="px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium rounded-lg text-mapa-ink/70 hover:text-mapa-ink transition-all cursor-pointer"
							>
								Geographic Map
							</button>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="text-xs text-mapa-clay hidden sm:block">
						<span class="inline-block w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-rose-600 mr-1 align-middle"></span>
						Physical Kilometer Posts
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- VIEW 1: Schematic Milestone Chain Container -->
				<div id="schematic-view-container" class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
					<div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-3 mb-4 border-b border-mapa-contour/50">
						<div>
							<h3 id="schematic-corridor-title" class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-mapa-ink">
								MacArthur Highway Milestone Chain
							</h3>
							<p class="text-xs text-mapa-clay">
								Click any concrete milestone along the corridor ribbon to inspect its town and landmarks.
							</p>
						</div>
						<span id="schematic-total-km" class="text-[11px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour text-mapa-green">
							488.0 Total KM
						</span>
					</div>

					<!-- Milestone Chain Nodes -->
					<div id="milestone-chain-list" class="space-y-3 max-h-[620px] overflow-y-auto pr-2 custom-scrollbar">
						<!-- Injected via JavaScript based on selected Highway -->
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- VIEW 2: Geographic Leaflet Map Container -->
				<div id="geo-view-container" class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-2xl p-4 shadow-xs hidden">
					<div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-3 mb-2 border-b border-mapa-contour/50">
						<div>
							<h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-mapa-ink">Geographic Highway Marker Map</h3>
							<p class="text-xs text-mapa-clay">CartoDB Voyager map showing exact milestone coordinates</p>
						</div>
						<div class="text-xs text-mapa-clay flex items-center gap-2">
							<span class="inline-block w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-rose-600"></span>
							<span>Milestone Posts</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Map Div -->
					<div id="km-map" class="w-full h-[580px] rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-mapa-contour/60"></div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- Educational Guide: How to Read a Philippine Kilometer Post -->
		<section class="mb-14 font-sans">
			<div class="border-b border-mapa-contour/50 pb-3 mb-6">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-mapa-ink">
					How to Read a Philippine Highway Kilometer Post
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-mapa-clay mt-1">
					Standard anatomy and official DPWH Highway Design Guidelines (Design Guidelines, Criteria and Standards - DGCS).
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-sm">
				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-2xs">
					<div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-600/15 text-emerald-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
						1
					</div>
					<h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-ink mb-1.5">
						The Top Cap (Destination & Target Distance)
					</h3>
					<p class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
						The upper semicircular or trapezoidal section indicates the <strong>name of the next major city or town</strong> followed by the distance in kilometers to its municipal hall or provincial plaza (e.g. <code>ANGELES 17</code> means Angeles City center is 17 km ahead).
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-2xs">
					<div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-600/15 text-blue-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
						2
					</div>
					<h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-ink mb-1.5">
						The Center Body (Distance from KM 0)
					</h3>
					<p class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
						The large, prominent numeral preceded by <code>KM</code> displays your <strong>exact physical distance from Kilometer Zero</strong> (e.g. <code>KM 66</code> indicates you are precisely 66.0 kilometers away from the Rizal Monument at Luneta Park in Manila).
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-2xs">
					<div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-rose-600/15 text-rose-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
						3
					</div>
					<h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-ink mb-1.5">
						The Base Band (DPWH District & Route)
					</h3>
					<p class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
						The red painted base (or yellow for provincial roads) often bears embossed lettering denoting the <strong>DPWH Engineering District Office</strong> and national highway classification code (e.g. <code>N2</code> for primary roads or <code>DEO-PAMPANGA</code>).
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) Section -->
		<section class="border-t border-mapa-contour/50 pt-10 font-sans">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-6">
				Frequently Asked Questions About Philippine Kilometer Markers
			</h2>

			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm">
				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">Where is the primary Kilometer Zero (KM 0) in the Philippines?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						The primary and official geodetic Kilometer Zero for the entire island of Luzon is located across from the <strong>José Rizal Monument in Luneta Park (Rizal Park), City of Manila</strong>. Distance measurements for all major highways—including MacArthur Highway, Maharlika Highway, Manila South Road, and Aguinaldo Highway—originate from this spot.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">Does Mindanao have its own Kilometer Zero?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						Yes. Mindanao’s historical Kilometer Zero is located in <strong>Marawi City, Lanao del Sur</strong>, along the shoreline of Lake Lanao near Banggolo Bridge. It served as the original survey baseline when the trans-Mindanao highway network was surveyed and constructed.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">Why are kilometer markers important for cyclists and emergency responders?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						In rural stretches where cellular GPS data may experience dead zones, physical kilometer posts provide an unambiguous, universally recognized location stamp. Philippine National Police (PNP), DPWH, and ambulance dispatchers (911) frequently use KM posts to pinpoint road accident locations.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">What are the Bataan Death March Kilometer Markers?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						These are 138 specially designed white obelisk memorial markers erected to honor Filipino and American soldiers forced into the 1942 Bataan Death March during World War II. They start at KM 00 in Mariveles and KM 00 in Bagac, continuing through Pampanga up to San Fernando (KM 102) and Capas, Tarlac.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

